1. A marine wave redirection device comprising:  

a frame assembly including a first frame body and a second frame body, the first frame body and the second frame body being connected to one another or formed integrally with one another;  

wherein the first frame body defines a first frame angle configured to orient at least a portion of the marine wave redirection device relative to an incoming wave direction;  

wherein the second frame body defines a second frame angle different from the first frame angle and configured to redirect at least a portion of wave energy laterally, upwardly, downwardly, or a combination thereof;  

a plurality of anchor feet coupled to or formed with the frame assembly, the anchor feet being configured to engage a seabed, shoreline, floor, wall, support surface, or other marine installation surface to resist displacement of the marine wave redirection device; and  

a blade mounted on an upper portion of the frame assembly, the blade being positioned and angled to intercept water moving over or against the frame assembly and to redirect at least a portion of the water away from an original wave travel path.
